---
import PersonalVault from "@/layouts/PersonalVault.astro";
import { withBase } from "@/utils/path";
---

<PersonalVault
	title="Overview"
	description="Personal Vault is Henrique Bastos's private application for collecting and reviewing meeting notes and transcripts."
>
	<h1>Personal Vault</h1>
	<p>
		I am Henrique Bastos. I am building Personal Vault to collect Google Meet notes and transcripts
		from my Google Workspace accounts into my private Obsidian vault.
	</p>
	<p>
		This application is for my own use. There is no public registration, and this website does not
		collect Google account credentials.
	</p>

	<h2>1 What the application does</h2>
	<p>
		Personal Vault uses Calendar events and email notifications to find meeting documents. It saves
		the available notes and transcripts as separate files, with their source references.
	</p>
	<p>
		I can then review the files, create summaries, or turn a transcript into an illustrated
		storyboard with AI assistance. Notes are not treated as verbatim transcripts.
	</p>

	<h2>2 Google account access</h2>
	<p>
		I authorize each account separately through Google's OAuth consent screen. The application
		requests read-only access to Calendar events, the calendar list, Google Docs, and Gmail, plus
		basic account identity.
	</p>
	<p>
		These permissions cover more than meeting content. The import process selects the relevant
		events, messages, and documents. It does not request permission to send email or change Calendar
		events or Google Docs.
	</p>

	<h2>3 Storage and privacy</h2>
	<p>
		Imported content goes into my local vault and may also enter Git history and Obsidian Sync.
		Selected content may be sent to AI services for the processing I request.
	</p>
	<p>
		Meeting content is not published on this website. See the <a
			href={withBase("/apps/personal-vault/privacy/")}>privacy policy</a
		> for data handling, retention, and deletion, and the <a
			href={withBase("/apps/personal-vault/terms/")}>terms of use</a
		> for the application's limits.
	</p>
</PersonalVault>
